// plantrx server address — copy to plantrx_config.h and fill in.
// The real file is gitignored: the address is per-greenhouse, not per-firmware,
// since the server runs on whatever box is on that site's LAN.
//
// What is here is the SEED, not the only source. sitecfg.cpp is the one file
// that reads these, and it writes anything non-empty into NVS on boot so that a
// later image built with these blank - which is what CI builds, because a public
// artifact must not carry a secret - keeps the site it was provisioned with.
// Fill this in, flash once over USB, and every update after that can arrive over
// the air with nothing in it. sitecfg.h has the full rule.
#pragma once

// Base URL of the plantrx server, without a trailing slash. Empty means the
// uplink is not configured at all: plantrx_configured() goes false, the client
// never opens a socket, and the panel runs on its local rule engine.
//
// BOTH SCHEMES WORK, AND THIS ONE LINE IS WHAT DECIDES ENCRYPTION FOR THE WHOLE GREENHOUSE.
// https:// makes every server socket on all three boards TLS with a pinned root; http:// makes
// them plaintext. Nothing else in the firmware chooses - shared/srvurl.h parses the scheme and
// shared/srvconn.h hands out the matching client, so there is no per-site override to forget.
//
// It reaches the two boards without a console by itself: sitecfg.cpp lets a non-empty value here
// overwrite what NVS holds, and src/nodeota.cpp sends the panel's own stored URL to the sensor
// node and the camera in every update command. So flashing the panel moves the fleet.
//
// This comment used to say "http:// only ... TLS would buy nothing here". That was wrong twice:
// the token and every reading cross the public internet rather than a closed LAN, and TLS was
// measured on this hardware at 1.84s a handshake with chain verification and no lasting DRAM
// cost. See the note at the top of shared/srvurl.h for the measurements.
//
// A URL with any other scheme is treated as unconfigured rather than guessed at.
#define PLANTRX_BASE_URL "https://plantrx.example.org"

// Shared secret matching PLANTRX_TOKEN in the server's environment. Empty when
// the server runs without one (its auth dependency skips the check), which is
// the usual case on a closed greenhouse LAN.
#define PLANTRX_TOKEN ""
